	(text "Same circuit as the input limiter: limit ~0.65 V / R17\n= ~87 mA, enough for the tablet board (<= ~61 mA).\nGPIO5 high -> Q6 on -> Q4 base drive through R19.\nR18 holds Q4 off; R21 keeps Q6 off at reset.\nD4 SMBJ24A + C13 protect the cable output.\nVTAB_SENSE = TAB_OUT / 16 to GPIO1.\nQ4 tab = TAB_OUT: give it >= 1 cm2 of copper."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 193.04 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "1e78479b-ae88-5c10-bd02-493bd6b38dbf")
	)
	(text "ESP32-C3  +  PROG HEADER"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 161.29 118.11 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "30e15631-62d6-554c-9f1b-4eb0f65922a1")
	)
	(text "RELAY MODULE + TX SWITCH"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 16.51 26.67 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "501ae270-41cb-5990-8066-a234de3989ef")
	)
	(text "3.3 V BUCK  (LMR51606, 1.1 MHz PFM)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 237.49 26.67 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "6583017e-a75f-5743-9d1f-1c2fe2ffc078")
	)
	(text "Q1 AO3422 pulls POWER to GND through R2\n(3.3R pulse-rated): ~15 us pulses, like the\noriginal pad's Q2/R4. The gate is AC-coupled\n(C1, R4) so a crashed ESP32 can't hold the\nline low. D1 SMBJ30A clamps surges.\nJ1 pin 2 COMMON is this board's GND."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 85.09 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "71b96ffd-5fa6-5549-844e-249d4b7381d4")
	)
	(text "AUX INPUT + 5V_AUX"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 323.85 118.11 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "7e95a055-e370-516b-836d-1bf9f33a225b")
	)
	(text "IO2, IO8: strapping pull-ups.\nIO9 (BOOT) low at reset = download."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 284.48 203.2 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "91e06eb5-3254-5469-adcb-470c07772171")
	)
	(text "INPUT LIMITER (~105 mA) + RESERVOIR"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 97.79 26.67 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b1a893b5-9ad8-5519-a6c1-d64ed69d8bcc")
	)
	(text "EN divider R7/R8: on at VRES ~12.1 V, off at ~9.9 V, so the\nreservoir charges before the ESP32 starts.\nFeedback R11/R12 (69.8k / 22.1k): 3.33 V."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 238.76 83.82 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d29a8955-2e70-5c5d-a684-6ac0f29c8cea")
	)
	(text "AUX (from J1 pin 3) is always loaded with\nR1 10k to 5V_AUX, like the original pad's\nR66 10k to its 5 V rail.\n\nR24/R25 (330k / 100k) = AUX / 4.3 to GPIO0.\nC16 10 nF filters it."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 325.12 172.72 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d418ccd7-6688-57f6-a1dd-f9d991fc3102")
	)
	(text "Limit ~0.65 V / R5 = ~105 mA: about what the\noriginal pad drew. Q3 senses R5 and steals\nQ2's base current. D2 isolates the board from\nthe TX pulses. Q2 tab = VRES: give it >= 1 cm2.\nReservoir 2x 1000 uF + 2.2 uF (Wi-Fi bursts).\nVSENSE = VRES / 16 to GPIO3."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 99.06 95.25 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d84c95d1-b987-529b-9803-c8bba56d9c49")
	)
	(text "TABLET OUTPUT  (limiter 2, ~87 mA, switched by GPIO5)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 16.51 118.11 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "f8439b83-d7fb-5723-bfad-f9731f853a38")
	)
